        {
            "sentence_index": 14,
            "timestamp": {
                "start": 133.74,
                "end": 164.28
            },
            "transcript": "The most serious difficulty encountered in dealing with the present state and future development of aircraft is the rapidity with which that development proceeds, before a congressional committee last January, an official testified that grave delay in the manufacture of airplanes for the Army has been caused by the fact that types adopted a scant three months before had become obsolete because of experience on the European battlefields, and later inventions before the first machines could be completed.",
            "acoustic_emotion": {
                "angry": 1.4907039651777716,
                "calm": 0.8975471235155769,
                "disgust": 0.7911025376579179,
                "fearful": 1.1146514286170253,
                "happy": 1.2020072253729885,
                "neutral": 1.0813931684118343,
